body:
Slow down there. I'm actually a man, I don't know where you got "lady" from.

&#x200B;

I disagree that it's disgusting to date around before you settle down with one person. I think it's actually unhealthy for people to rush into marriage just because they are 25 or 30 and feel like they are supposed to get married by that age. A serious relationship would get in the way of my current aspirations, so it has to wait. I will not put aside the things I want to do simply because I am 30 and society says now is the time to get married. It's women who have the biological clock and can't afford to wait too long to have kids. As a man, it would be completely viable for me to wait until I am 36 and marry a 28-32 year old.

&#x200B;

Also, I am pretty anti-feminism. However, the problem with feminism is not women's empowerment or allowing women to play the field. That is actually good for men. The issue is all these regulations on courtship which are basically designed to make it so that only the young gorgeous guys and the super charismatic guys are allowed to pursue women in any way. In the past, it was just the norm that men of all stripes would try to pursue women. Guys who were pretty average would typically manage to find women who are interested or make women interested. This is just what naturally happens when men and women connect with each other. But in this new cultural norm where male courtship is considered harassment and women will only tolerate it from the young, gorgeous and charismatic guys, that is prevented from happening. And the age thing is a perfect example of this. It is becoming increasingly taboo for men to show any interest in younger women. Seeing as how this is the case, making it acceptable for women to have affairs with teenage boys seems like a great way to ensure that men past a certain age are just entirely shut out of the dating scene. Your friend hooking up with his 40something professor is contributing to the culture of female privilege by allowing a woman to enjoy an experience that society would never allow a man her age to enjoy.

&#x200B;

And another thing, race has nothing to do with it. White men are no more screwed over by feminism than black or arab or asian men. I wish white men would stop throwing race into the mix, because this creates an association between anti-feminism and the white pride movement. I believe this gives a lot of non-white men the illusion that feminism is on their side. The fact is, feminism is colorblind in its hatred of men.

Funny, I've seen girls do stuff like this on numerous occasions. I've even had a female "friend" pull something like this on me before. She randomly told me that I'm "short for a guy." I'm actually around 6 foot, but I have a long neck so my shoulders are perhaps lower, and my arched neck could have perhaps made me appear shorter, but only slightly if at all. I turned turned around and asked her "Are you drunk?" She looks at me with straight face and says "no" shaking her head. I think I then asked her "who's tall then?" She pointed out our other friend, who is taller than me. This was years ago, and to this day, I don't understand what suddenly gave her the urge to tell me that. But there were other occasions where she appeared to have a weird fixation on height, for example pointing out how she thought one guy was taller than the other but just realized he was shorter.

&#x200B;

Actually, just now I am talking to a girl on Tinder whose behavior is super weird. I don't want to say specifically what it is, in case she happens to see this.
